       "PRINCIPLE_WORKED_EXAMPLE",
       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS"
      ],
      "rationale": "Number names come last because they hide the places that the chart and expanded form show. The final word, such as thousandths, tells how many digits follow the point. Some names have no whole-number part, so the answer begins with 0.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Writing twenty-six thousandths as 0.26, without the zero that holds the tenths place.",
       "Writing \"and\" as a decimal point when it joins hundreds and tens, as in one hundred and five."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2015), Progressions for Number and Operations in Base Ten, K-5"
      ]
